[agent:result] Usage: hops job schedule [OPTIONS] NAME CRON
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]   Attach (or update) a Quartz cron schedule to ``name``.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]   The cron interval is the firing cadence. The data window the job consumes
[agent:result]   per fire is controlled by ``--start-offset-seconds`` / ``--end-offset-
[agent:result]   seconds`` (relative to the fire time). ``--catchup`` replays missed
[agent:result]   intervals after an outage; ``--max-catchup-runs`` caps how many missed
[agent:result]   intervals are replayed.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]   Args:     ctx: Click context.     name: Job name.     cron: Quartz cron
[agent:result]   expression, or a shorthand (@hourly, @daily,         @midnight, @weekly,
[agent:result]   @monthly, @yearly).     start_time: ISO timestamp for the first trigger.
[agent:result]   end_time: ISO timestamp for the last trigger.     start_offset_seconds: Per-
[agent:result]   fire offset for ``HOPS_START_TIME``.     end_offset_seconds: Per-fire offset
[agent:result]   for ``HOPS_END_TIME``.     catchup: Replay missed fires on recovery.
[agent:result]   max_active_runs: Upper bound on concurrent executions.     max_catchup_runs:
